A cantilever 3D printer is a type of 3D printer that uses a single-sided support arm to hold and move the print bed or printing mechanism. Unlike traditional 3D printers that use two support rails or frames on both sides, a cantilever design supports the moving part from only one side.

Features of a Cantilever 3D Printer
Single-arm support for the X-axis or print bed
Compact and lightweight design
Easier to assemble and maintain
Usually quieter and portable
Advantages
Saves space because of its smaller frame
Lower manufacturing cost
Good for beginners and small printing projects
Faster movement due to lighter structure
Disadvantages
Less stable for large or heavy prints
May experience slight wobbling at high speeds
Limited print size compared to dual-support printers
Common Uses

Cantilever 3D printers are commonly used for:

Educational projects
Hobby printing
Prototype creation
Small household items and decorations
